Implement a new pure TypeScript catalog cleanup API:

```ts
export type ArtifactKind = "script" | "style";
export interface Artifact { readonly path: string; readonly kind: ArtifactKind; readonly deleted: boolean; }
export interface Bundle { readonly name: string; readonly kind: ArtifactKind; readonly artifacts: readonly Artifact[]; }
export interface Catalog { readonly root: string; readonly bundles: readonly Bundle[]; }
export interface CleanupOptions { readonly allowedSuffixes: readonly string[]; readonly root: string; }
export function cleanCatalog(catalog: Catalog, options: CleanupOptions): Catalog;
```

The function must not mutate or reuse any input bundle, artifact, or array. `root` must be nonblank after trimming. Allowed suffixes must begin with `.` and comparisons are case-insensitive; invalid suffixes throw `RangeError`. Normalize the output root by removing trailing `/` characters, except that `/` remains `/`. For every artifact, discard it if `deleted` is true or its path does not end in an allowed suffix. Retained artifact paths become `normalizedRoot + "/" + relativePath`, with leading `/` characters removed from the original path. An empty artifact path is malformed and throws `RangeError`. Preserve bundle and artifact order. Remove a bundle when no artifacts remain. Also remove any retained artifact whose kind differs from its bundle kind. Duplicate paths remain duplicated. An empty suffix list produces a catalog with no bundles.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

